From: LukeOkk <85941941+LukeOkk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 05:03:37 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] compiler: arm64 code for a heap reference base (SteamARM,
 HYPOTHESIS)

HYPOTHESIS, UNTESTED: not compiled, no code generated or run.

Upstream arm64 code keeps a reference in a W register and dereferences its
X view, relying on the zero extension of 32-bit writes; heap poisoning hooks
mark the heap loads and stores. With kTargetHeapReferenceBase != 0 the
invariant becomes: a reference in a core register is a full pointer (null
0); in memory it is the low 32 bits. Compression is the existing 32-bit
store. Decompression (Arm64Assembler::DecompressHeapReference) is
"cbz w, 1f; orr x, x, #base; 1:", or one ORR when the value cannot be null;
it is idempotent on a full pointer.

Changed (numbers from SteamARM's patches/art-heap-base/count_sites.py):

- the load hook: MaybeUnpoisonHeapReference() also decompresses (24 call
  sites, C1), and so does MaybeGenerateReadBarrierSlow()'s no-barrier path;
- Baker read barriers: field, array, acquire and CAS old-value loads
  decompress after the return label, where the not-gray LDR, the
  introspection entrypoint's W move and the thunk all arrive (16 call
  sites, C4); the thunk layout and BAKER_MARK_INTROSPECTION_*_LDR_OFFSET do
  not change;
- GC roots (declaring class, .bss, JIT roots): GenerateGcRootFieldLoad()
  decompresses at its end (5 call sites, C3); the GC-root thunk decompresses
  the root before reading its lock word (C5);
- 32-bit values that are addresses in the window: .data.bimg.rel.ro entries
  (classes, strings, boot image ArtMethods), JIT boot image literals and
  JIT root-table slot addresses (C6); their DCHECKed 32-bit casts become
  compressions;
- Thread fields that hold objects: exception load and clear, peer load, as
  64 bits (C7);
- address arithmetic on references: array element addresses, far and
  acquire Baker field bases, UnsafeGet, vector addresses, card marking (C8);
  HIntermediateAddress (a kInt32 value the register allocator may spill as
  32 bits) is no longer extracted;
- moves: register moves of references keep 64 bits, reloads from 32-bit
  spill slots and stack arguments decompress, and the parallel move
  resolver passes the reference type (C9); HSelect of references selects X
  registers; an interface call's receiver reloaded from the stack is
  decompressed.

HeapOperand() and the 61 dereferences through it (C10) are unchanged: they
use the X view, which now holds the full pointer. Card marking uses the full
address, matching the runtime's card table over the window.

